{#- The sections of the literature page, also sections of the full report. `c`: tsbench.report.literature.context();
`h`: the heading level of a section (h2 on the page, h3 inside the full report); the system cards take the next one.
Figures of kind parity and relerr are drawn by literature.js, the others by runtime.js. -#}
{% from "_macros.html.j2" import fig, legend_html %}
{% from "literature_macros.html.j2" import doi_text, ref_row, run_row, bands_table, tip_table, rate_table, cond_legend %}

{% macro lit_facts(c) -%}
<dl class="facts">
{% for f in c.facts %}
<div><dt>{{ f.name }}</dt><dd>{{ f.value }}</dd><dd class="cap">{{ f.caption }}</dd></div>
{% endfor %}
</dl>
{% if c.notes %}
<ul class="warn">
{% for n in c.notes %}
<li>{{ n }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_accuracy(c, h="h2") -%}
<section id="lit-accuracy"><{{ h }}>Accuracy on the literature tasks</{{ h }}>
<p>Share of correct answers among the evaluable runs per model and condition, with the 95 % interval of a task-clustered
bootstrap: the k repetitions of a task are not independent, so tasks are resampled and the runs of a task kept together. A row with fewer than five evaluable runs
shows its counts only: with two runs the interval spans at least 34 points.</p>{{ legend_html() }}
{% for g in c.groups %}
{% set table %}{{ rate_table(g.table) }}{% endset %}
{{ fig("rate", {"rows": g.rows, "left": 118}, g.title, g.alt, table) }}{{ table }}
{% endfor %}
</section>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_parity(c, h="h2") -%}
<section id="lit-parity"><{{ h }}>Parity: model and paper against the oracle</{{ h }}>{{ cond_legend(c.cond_items) }}<div class="bpgrid">
{% for f in c.parity %}
{% set table %}{{ tip_table(f.tips) }}{% endset %}
{{ fig("parity", f.spec, f.caption, f.alt, table, "", "litfig") }}
{% endfor %}
</div></section>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_relerr(c, h="h2") -%}
<section id="lit-relerr"><{{ h }}>Relative error per system</{{ h }}>{{ cond_legend(c.cond_items) }}<div class="bpgrid wide1">
{% for f in c.relerr %}
{% set table %}{{ tip_table(f.tips) }}{% endset %}
{{ fig("relerr", f.spec, f.caption, f.alt, table, "", "litfig") }}
{% endfor %}
</div></section>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_systems(c, h="h2") -%}
{% set sub = "h3" if h == "h2" else "h4" %}
<section id="lit-systems"><{{ h }}>Systems: paper, oracle and model answers</{{ h }}>
<p>Per system the band energies with their terms, the source and the reference rows (paper, oracle, tolerance),
then every model answer. Δ oracle and Δ paper are relative errors (answer − reference) / reference; the paper columns
compare only Dq, Dq/B and C/B, because the paper does not give B and C. Grey rows (HTTP 429 or another API error) do
not count.</p>{{ legend_html(c.card_keys) }}
{% for s in c.systems %}
<article class="sys" id="{{ s.ident }}"><{{ sub }}>{{ s.system }} <span class="muted">· d{{ s.d }}, {{ s.geometry }} ·
{{ s.short }}, {{ s.id }}</span></{{ sub }}>
<div class="syshead"><div>{{ bands_table(s.bands, c.unit) }}</div><div>
<p class="src"><b>Source:</b> {{ doi_text(s.source) }}</p>
<p class="src"><b>Table references:</b> {{ s.refs }}</p>
{% if s.location %}
<p class="src"><b>Location:</b> {{ s.location }}; assignment: {{ s.assignment }}</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="src"><b>Oracle:</b> {{ s.oracle }}{% if s.cb_fixed %}; C/B fixed {{ s.cb_fixed }}{% endif %}</p>
<p class="src"><b>Runs:</b> {{ s.summary }}</p></div></div>
<div class="scroll"><table class="wide runs"><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Cond.</th><th>Effort</th><th>k</th><th>Status</th>
<th>Dq ({{ c.unit }})</th><th>B ({{ c.unit }})</th><th>C ({{ c.unit }})</th><th>Dq/B</th><th>C/B</th>
<th>ΔDq oracle</th><th>ΔB oracle</th><th>ΔC oracle</th><th>ΔDq paper</th><th>Δ(Dq/B) paper</th><th>Δ(C/B) paper</th>
<th>Run</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in s.ref_rows %}
{{ ref_row(r) }}
{% endfor %}
{% for r in s.runs %}
{{ run_row(r) }}
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div></article>
{% endfor %}
</section>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_exclusions(c, h="h2") -%}
{% if c.exclusions %}
<section id="lit-excluded"><{{ h }}>Excluded systems</{{ h }}><p>These systems of the table are not tasks: the fit
runs into a bound of the search range, is not unique or does not fit the model (rules in the rubric). Shown are the
reason, the oracle fit from the rubric and the values the paper reports.</p><div class="scroll"><table class="wide">
<thead><tr><th>System</th><th>d</th><th>Reason</th>
<th>Oracle fit (rubric, {{ c.unit }})</th><th>Paper Dq ({{ c.unit }})</th><th>Paper Dq/B</th><th>Paper C/B</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for x in c.exclusions %}
<tr><td>{{ x.system }}</td><td>d{{ x.d }}</td><td>{{ x.reason }}</td><td>{{ x.fit }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.dq }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.dqb }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.cb }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div></section>
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro lit_methods(c, h="h2") -%}
<section id="lit-methods"><{{ h }}>Methods: where the numbers come from</{{ h }}><ul>
<li><b>Paper</b>: Dq, Dq/B and C/B as printed in the paper's table (columns <code>Dq_cm-1</code>,
<code>DqB_reported</code>, <code>CB_reported</code>, auxiliary diagram <code>DqB_aux_diagram</code>,
<code>CB_aux_diagram</code>). The paper does not give B and C; they are derived as B = Dq / (Dq/B) and
C = (C/B) · B. Paper values never enter the scoring.</li>
<li><b>Oracle</b> (the reference of the task, never taken from the paper): for <code>literature_all</code> and
<code>literature_new</code> a least-squares fit of (Dq, B[, C]) with the forward model <code>tanabesugano</code> to
the assigned band energies (C only when the bands determine it, else C/B = 4.5 fixed); for <code>experimental</code>
the closed-form expressions for two or three bands. The oracle belongs to the task, not to the system: one system can
have different reference values in two classes.</li>
<li><b>Tolerance</b> (relative to the oracle): Dq {{ c.tolerance.Dq }} %, B {{ c.tolerance.B }} %,
C {{ c.tolerance.C }} % (only when C is asked for). An answer is correct when every requested value lies within its
tolerance; check and cross in the cells show it per value.</li>
<li><b>Model answers</b>: one row per run (model × condition × effort × k), scored in memory with
<code>tsbench.score.score</code>. Runs with HTTP 429 or another API error (grey) enter no rate and no
figure.</li>
<li><b>Repetitions</b>: the k repetitions of a cell are not independent (same task, same model), so the intervals
resample tasks, not runs.</li>
<li>The excluded systems and the rules behind them are in the rubric of the task set
(<code>src/tsbench/data/tasks/rubric.md</code>).</li></ul></section>
{%- endmacro %}
